Request Mapping :
Request Mapping is used to connect a URL with a Controller method.
Syntax : @RequestMapping("/url")
Example : 
@Controller
public class WebsiteController 
{
    @RequestMapping("/home")
    public String home() 
    {
        return "home";
    }
    @RequestMapping("/about")
    public String about() 
    {
        return "about";
    }
    @RequestMapping("/contact")
    public String contact() 
    {
        return "contact";
    }
}

Request Methods :
| Method | Purpose       |
| ------ | ------------- |
| GET    | Retrieve data |
| POST   | Send data     |
| PUT    | Update data   |
| DELETE | Delete data   |


@GetMapping is used to handle HTTP GET requests.(display data from the server)
@PostMapping is used to handle HTTP POST requests.(send data from the client to the server)
@PutMapping is used to handle HTTP PUT requests.(update existing data)
@DeleteMapping is used to handle HTTP DELETE requests.(remove data from the server)

| Annotation       | Action | Meaning              |
| ---------------- | ------ | -------------------- |
| `@GetMapping`    | Read   | Get/View data        |
| `@PostMapping`   | Create | Add new data         |
| `@PutMapping`    | Update | Modify existing data |
| `@DeleteMapping` | Delete | Remove data          |

Form Handling :
Form Handling is the process of collecting data from a user through a form and processing it in the Controller.

@RequestParam is a Spring MVC annotation used to receive data sent from the client and store it in a controller method parameter.

Data Binding is the process of automatically transferring data from a web form into a Java object.

Data Binding vs @RequestParam :
| @RequestParam                | Data Binding                    |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Used for few fields          | Used for many fields            |
| Receives one value at a time | Receives entire object          |
| Lengthy for large forms      | Cleaner code                    |
| Suitable for simple forms    | Suitable for registration forms |
